{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConvexPolygonShape2D","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A 2D convex polygon shape, intended for use in physics. Used internally in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D","type":"reference"},{"text":" when it’s in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/solids","type":"reference"},{"text":" mode.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"solid","type":"text"}]},{"text":", which means it detects collisions from objects that are fully inside it, unlike ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D"},{"text":" which is hollow. This makes it more suitable for both detection and physics.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Convex decomposition:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A concave polygon can be split up into several convex polygons. This allows dynamic physics bodies to have complex concave collisions (at a performance cost) and can be achieved by using several ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" nodes or by using the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" node in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/solids","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" mode. To generate a collision polygon from a sprite, select the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Sprite2D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" node, go to the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sprite2D","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" menu that appears above the viewport, and choose ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create Polygon2D Sibling","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Performance:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is faster to check collisions against compared to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", but it is slower than primitive collision shapes such as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CircleShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RectangleShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Its use should generally be limited to medium-sized objects that cannot have their collision accurately represented by primitive shapes."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A 2D convex polygon shape used for physics collision.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/convexpolygonshape2d"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"ConvexPolygonShape2D","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"}